messages:
elaine: Quick sync — I opened a PR to consolidate 429 + timeout + context-limit guidance into a single error-reference page. Wanted to get reviewers before we start adding SDK snippets and migration notes: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/2345

mike: Nice, thanks. Does the PR include Node/Python SDK backoff examples or just pseudo-code?

elaine: It has a Python backoff example but the Node one is rough. Current Node snippet in the draft: 
```js
// retry on 429 with exponential backoff (pseudo)
const retry = async (fn) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn()
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status !== 429) throw err
      await sleep(Math.pow(2, i) * 100)
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted')
}
```
Not sure about surfacing Retry-After header handling.

jade: I can take the Node snippet. Also suggestion: we should explicitly call out context-window trimming as a fallback strategy (not just model fallback). Customers need a concrete example for prompt chunking + re-assembly. Might add a tiny example and link to the new optimize guide.

sam: Strong +1 on the Retry-After detail — we've had customers who see 429s from upstream proxies and think the model is throttling. Could we add a diagnostic curl command to show headers so they can tell the difference? e.g.
```bash
curl -I -s -D - https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | sed -n '1,20p'
```
That helps debug if Retry-After or X-RateLimit-* headers are present.

mike: Also for timeouts: show a graceful-degrade flow (summary-only response or cached embedding fallback) and link to the console rollout example for automatic fallback policies. I'll push a tiny blurb into the PR.

deploy-bot: CI: docs build succeeded — 12/12 checks passed :white_check_mark:

elaine: Awesome, thanks everyone. @jade please leave a review when you have the Node snippet ready, @mike add the rollout link. Plan: merge by EOD if no blockers. :thumbsup:
